      "id": "make",
      "name": "Make",
      "category": "ShapeInstance",
      "signature": "Make(In Shape Idx, In Geometry)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "In Shape Idx",
          "type": "Int"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Geometry",
          "type": "FImplicitObjectPtr&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "TUniquePtr<FShapeInstanceProxy>",
      "docs": "NOTE: FShapeInstance is a Physics-Thread object.\nSee FShapeInstanceProxy for the game-thread equivalent\nFShapeInstance contains the per-shape data associated with a single shape on a particle.\nThis contains data like the collision / query filters, material properties etc.\nEvery particle holds one FShapeInstance object for each geometry they use.\nIf the particle has a Union of geometries there will be one FShapeInstance\nfor each geometry in the union. (Except ClusteredUnions - these are not flattened\nbecause they contain their own query acceleration structure.)\nNOTE: keep size to a minimum. There can be millions of these in s scene.\nNOTE: this version has reduced-memory material storage compared to FShapeInstanceProxy,\nbut increased cost when switching from a single-material to a multi-material shape\n(though this should not be happening much if at all)."
    },
